{
  "meta": {
    "generated": "2026-10-12",
    "description": "Reference along-river distances for testing OSM-based river chainage. expectedKm = difference of IMGW 'kilometr_biegu_rzeki' (distance from the river mouth) between two gauging stations on the same river.",
    "sources": [
      "https://danepubliczne.imgw.pl/api/data/hydro (IMGW-PIB public data, fields lat/lon/kilometr_biegu_rzeki)"
    ],
    "caveats": [
      "IMGW km is measured from the river MOUTH. It is NOT the navigational kilometrage of the Wisła (from Przemsza) or Odra (from Opawa).",
      "Station coordinates have 4 decimals (~10 m) and mark the gauge, which usually sits on the bank, not on the centreline: snap to the river line before measuring and check snap distance (< ~150 m).",
      "IMGW kilometrage is old and built on official hydrographic geometry; after channel regulation real length can differ by a few percent. Treat relTolerance as the acceptance band, not as an error of your code.",
      "Tags mark pairs that are hard for OSM: lakes, reservoirs, multi-channel reaches, canals. Expect larger deviations there.",
      "Gwda: only one IMGW gauge (Ptusza) was captured; the second endpoint is the Gwda–Noteć confluence (km 0) with approximate coordinates."
    ],
    "tolerancePolicy": "relTolerance 0.03 by default, 0.06 for tags: mountain, gorge, anastomosing, multi_channel, braided, lake_river, canal_ambiguity, derived_endpoint"
  },
